---
import ContentLayout from "astro-theme-university/layouts/ContentLayout.astro";
import { withBase } from "astro-theme-university/url";
import SessionsGrid from "../../components/SessionsGrid.astro";
import { sessionLabels, siteConfig } from "../../site-config";
---

<ContentLayout
  title={sessionLabels.plural}
  description={`The twelve-week teaching schedule: what happens in each ${sessionLabels.singular.toLowerCase()}, what to prepare, and what leaves the room.`}
  {...siteConfig}
>
  <p>
    Thursdays, in the field. A Round is a visit with a brief: where to go, what
    to count, how to take the notes, and what has to be true by the time you
    leave. The name carries both senses — a round of visits, and a round at the
    bar.
  </p>
  <p>
    Read the brief <em>before</em> you go. Several of them fix a rule you have to
    commit to in writing beforehand, because a rule invented while counting
    bends towards the answer you expected. Three Rounds are not site visits at
    all: week 3 is indoors, week 6 is your own network, and week 11 is a desk.
  </p>
  <p>
    Where you may observe and where you may not is not negotiable and is set out
    in full on the <a href={withBase("/policies/")}>policies page</a>. Read it before the
    first Round, not before the seventh.
  </p>
  <SessionsGrid />
</ContentLayout>
